id: pm-jev-w1zj
title: Preserve partial evaluation receipts and call counts on interruption
description: "An endpoint timeout stops evaluation safely before configuration persistence, but completed observations and the attempted-call count are not returned. A bounded run then needs an external access log to reconstruct its spent budget. Follow-up: emit a redacted partial receipt and explicit attempted/completed counts on failure or interruption, without fitting or saving from incomplete evidence."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: deferred,eval,"gh:unbraind/pm-jev#45",reliability
created_at: "2026-10-18T03:58:44.531Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T08:26:14.232Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T08:26:14.221Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-18T06:59:58.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "A synthetic two-request run failing on the second request reports two attempts and one completed example, preserves hashes and validated observations, makes no configuration write and does not retry; the failure receipt excludes source text and local paths."
parent: pm-jev-0w3q
resolution: "Delivered by https://github.com/unbraind/pm-jev/pull/24 (merge b479dd093e30, head 366d42c8b549)"
expected_result: "A synthetic two-request run failing on the second request reports two attempts and one completed example, preserves hashes and validated observations, makes no configuration write and does not retry; the failure receipt excludes source text and local paths."
actual_result: "Merged at 2026-10-18T06:59:58Z; no readable required checks, so every completed head check run had to succeed, be neutral or be skipped; successful checks: CodeQL, CodeRabbit, codeql, test (22), test (26)"
